# Performance, Safelist, Purging

## Overview
Tailwind CSS v4 uses `@source` for content scanning and safelisting for dynamic classes.

## @source Configuration

```css
@source "./src/**/*.{html,js,ts,jsx,tsx}";
@source "./components/**/*.md";
```

## Safelist Patterns

```css
@tailwind utilities;

/* Safelist dynamic variants */
@source inline("bg-[red-500]") "bg-*";
@source inline("text-size-[*]") "text-*";
```

Or in config:
```css
@utility safelist {
  /* classes */
}
```

## Critical CSS

Extract above-the-fold styles:

```css
@layer critical {
  .hero { /* styles */ }
}
```

## Best Practices

- Limit `@source` globs to actual content
- Use inline safelist for generated classes
- Avoid `*` safelists; be specific
- Purge unused CSS in production
- Measure bundle size with `tailwindcss --stats`
- Use `content-visibility` for offscreen sections
- Defer non-critical utilities

## Bundle Optimization

- Prefer utilities over custom CSS when possible
- Reuse component classes via CVA
- Avoid arbitrary values in loops
- Tree-shake unused variants
